2026-09-22T11:24:03.3598633Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3598856Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3598933Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599034Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599106Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599208Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599286Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599384Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599471Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599579Z             return x + 1
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599686Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599757Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599853Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3599954Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600029Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600107Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600194Z     To execute it::
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600268Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600353Z         $ pytest
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600516Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600609Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600682Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600782Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3600861Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601000Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601171Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601248Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601341Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601430Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601526Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601626Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601700Z     
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601811Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-09-22T11:24:03.3601963Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
